.TH LPS 1 "September 2026" "authd" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lps \- administer the Peios local principal store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lps
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lps
is the administration client for
.BR lpsd (8).
It does not open the principal database itself; every operation is authorized
and performed by the daemon over
.IR /run/lpsd/admin.sock .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List every principal.
.TP
.BI show " name"
Show one principal in full.
.TP
.B domain
Print the machine's domain SID.
.TP
.BI add " [name] [options]"
Create a principal.  Options are
.BR \-\-group ,
.BR \-\-primary-group ,
.BR \-\-home ,
.BR \-\-shell ,
.BR \-\-display-name ,
.BR \-\-disabled ,
.BR \-\-no-password ,
and
.BR \-\-no-prompt .
.TP
.BI remove " name"
Delete a principal.  RIDs are never reused; disabling an account is usually
safer because descriptors may continue to name its SID.
.TP
.BI enable " name"
Permit a principal to log on.
.TP
.BI disable " name"
Refuse logon while retaining the principal and SID.
.TP
.BI password " name"
Set a principal's password, as an administrator.  A principal changes their
own with
.BR passwd (1).
Setting material does not change credential policy.
.TP
.BI key\ list " name"
Show credential policy and enrolled key IDs, SHA256 fingerprints, labels and creation times.
.TP
.BI key\ add " name public-key-file [label]"
Enroll an Ed25519 or RSA (3072 to 8192 bits) public key. Duplicate keys, key
options, certificates and private keys are refused. Enrollment does not change policy.
.TP
.BI key\ remove " name key-id"
Remove an enrolled key by its 32-digit hexadecimal ID. Removing the last key
does not enable password or no-credential access. Existing sessions remain live.
.TP
.BI policy " name password|key|either|none|denied"
Select explicitly which credentials may authenticate this principal.
The none policy allows access without a credential and is intended only for
explicit development fixtures. Missing permitted material always fails closed.
.TP
.BI set " name [options]"
Change profile fields using
.BR \-\-home ,
.BR \-\-shell ,
.BR \-\-display-name ,
or
.BR \-\-primary-group .
.TP
.B group list
List local groups.
.TP
.BI group\ create " name"
Create a local group.
.TP
.BI group\ delete " name"
Delete an unused local group.
.TP
.BI group\ add " name group"
Add a principal to a group.
.TP
.BI group\ remove " name group"
Remove a principal from a group.
.TP
.BI claim\ set " name claim type [value ...]"
Set a claim.  Supported types are int64, uint64, boolean, string, sid, and
octet.
.TP
.BI claim\ remove " name claim"
Remove a claim.
.SH SECURITY
.B \-\-no-password
creates a principal that authenticates with no credential.  It is intended for
explicit disposable-image bootstrap policy, not normal production accounts.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR login (1),
.BR authd (8),
.BR lpsd (8)
